  "text": "Allergies:\nPenicillins / kapak\n\nChief Complaint:\nDyspnea\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nMr. ___ is a ___ year old male with metastatic melanoma with\nBRAF V600 mutation who presents with progressive dyspnea.\n\nOf note, the patient was recently admitted at ___ from \n___\nwith dyspnea where ___ was found to have progressive metastasis\nand an enlarged right pleural effusion. ___ underwent chest tube\nplacement with improvement of symptoms. ___ was initiated on\ndabrafenib and trametinib.\n\nSince discharge the patient has had continued fatigue and\nlethargy with progressive dyspnea on exertion for the last 2\nweek.s However, 2 days prior to presentation, ___ noticed a\nsignificant increase in his symptoms, having significant dyspnea\nwith walking to the bathroom. This was associated with increased\nabdominal pain in his LUQ and nausea with decreased PO intake.\n\n___ has had no fevers or chills. ___ notes intermittent headache.\nNo vision changes. No chest pain. No vomiting, diarrhea or\nconstipation.\n\nDue to progression of his symptoms her presented to the ED for\nfurther evaluation.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nMetastatic melanoma\nmalignant R pleural effusion",
